{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Stress Pipeline Debug — PSS-10 Correlation Validation\"\n",
        "format: html\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## What This Code Does\n",
        "\n",
        "This demo runs a simulation and tracks detailed per-agent data at each step: resilience, affect, stress, PSS-10, coping outcomes, challenge/hindrance values, and social influence. It computes step-by-step correlation matrices to validate that expected theoretical relationships — especially the negative correlation between resilience/affect and PSS-10 — hold throughout the simulation lifecycle.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Setup"
      ],
      "id": "847eea6b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: setup\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import sys\n",
        "import pathlib\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "\n",
        "demos_dir = pathlib.Path(os.getcwd())\n",
        "project_root = demos_dir.parents[2]\n",
        "sys.path.insert(0, str(project_root))\n",
        "\n",
        "from src.python.model import StressModel"
      ],
      "id": "setup",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Simulation and Data Collection"
      ],
      "id": "58f67d07"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: simulate\n",
        "n_agents, n_steps, seed = 20, 30, 42\n",
        "model = StressModel(N=n_agents, max_days=n_steps, seed=seed)\n",
        "\n",
        "records = []\n",
        "for step in range(n_steps):\n",
        "    model.step()\n",
        "    for i, agent in enumerate(model.agents):\n",
        "        records.append({\n",
        "            \"step\": step, \"agent\": i,\n",
        "            \"resilience\": agent.resilience,\n",
        "            \"affect\": agent.affect,\n",
        "            \"current_stress\": getattr(agent, \"current_stress\", 0),\n",
        "            \"pss10\": agent.pss10,\n",
        "        })\n",
        "\n",
        "df = pd.DataFrame(records)\n",
        "print(f\"Collected {len(df)} agent-step records ({n_steps} steps × {n_agents} agents)\")"
      ],
      "id": "simulate",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Correlation Over Time"
      ],
      "id": "17ba3c5c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: corr_time\n",
        "# Compute correlation at each step\n",
        "step_corrs = df.groupby(\"step\").apply(\n",
        "    lambda g: g[[\"resilience\", \"affect\", \"current_stress\", \"pss10\"]].corr().iloc[0, 3],\n",
        "    include_groups=False\n",
        ").reset_index()\n",
        "step_corrs.columns = [\"step\", \"resilience_pss10_corr\"]\n",
        "print(\"Resilience-PSS10 correlation by step:\")\n",
        "print(step_corrs.to_string(index=False))"
      ],
      "id": "corr_time",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Overall Correlation Matrix"
      ],
      "id": "c3428a7f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: corr_overall\n",
        "vars_ = [\"resilience\", \"affect\", \"current_stress\", \"pss10\"]\n",
        "corr_matrix = df[vars_].corr()\n",
        "print(corr_matrix.round(4))"
      ],
      "id": "corr_overall",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Correlation Trends"
      ],
      "id": "a8ba8088"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: plot\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
        "plt.plot(step_corrs[\"step\"], step_corrs[\"resilience_pss10_corr\"], marker=\".\", color=\"#3498db\")\n",
        "plt.axhline(y=0, color=\"gray\", linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.5)\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Step\"); plt.ylabel(\"Resilience-PSS10 Correlation\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Correlation Trend Over Simulation Steps\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "plot",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Why This Matters for the Simulation\n",
        "\n",
        "Debugging the stress pipeline is critical for ensuring model validity. The expected negative correlation between resilience and PSS-10 reflects the theoretical understanding that higher resilience buffers against perceived stress. If this correlation breaks down at any point in the pipeline, it indicates a bug or conceptual flaw in the stress processing mechanics. This demo provides the diagnostic tools needed to pinpoint such breakdowns."
      ],
      "id": "7181feb3"
    }
  ],
